split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உழப்பது","parts":[{"text":"உழப்பு","lemma":"உழப்பு","gloss":"suffer"},{"text":"அது","lemma":"அது","gloss":"pronominal suffix"}],"gloss":"suffering"},{"surface":"அன்றியும்","parts":[{"text":"அன்றி","lemma":"அன்றி","gloss":"besides"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and/even"}],"gloss":"besides"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மழையும்","parts":[{"text":"மழை","lemma":"மழை","gloss":"rain/cloud"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"the rain also"},{"surface":"தோழி","parts":[{"text":"தோழி","lemma":"தோழி","gloss":"friend"}],"gloss":"O friend"},{"surface":"மான்று","parts":[{"text":"மான்று","lemma":"மான்றல்","gloss":"having become dark/confused"}],"gloss":"having become dark"},{"surface":"பட்டன்றே","parts":[{"text":"பட்டன்றே","lemma":"பட்டன்றே","gloss":"has set/occurred indeed"}],"gloss":"has set/occurred indeed","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பட்ட","parts":[{"text":"பட்ட","lemma":"பட்ட","gloss":"which fell"}],"gloss":"which fell","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாரி","parts":[{"text":"மாரி","lemma":"மாரி","gloss":"rain"}],"gloss":"rain"},{"surface":"படாஅ","parts":[{"text":"படாஅ","lemma":"படு","gloss":"not falling"}],"gloss":"not falling"},{"surface":"கண்ணும்","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"time/place"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even at the time"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அவர்","parts":[{"text":"அவர்","lemma":"அவர்","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"he"},{"surface":"திறத்து","parts":[{"text":"திறத்து","lemma":"திறத்து","gloss":"concerning"}],"gloss":"concerning","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இரங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இரங்கு","lemma":"இரங்கு","gloss":"grieve/pity"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"which grieves"},{"surface":"நம்மினும்","parts":[{"text":"நம்","lemma":"நாம்","gloss":"us"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"comparative suffix"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"than/even"}],"gloss":"more than us"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நந்திறத்","parts":[{"text":"நந்திறத்","lemma":"நந்திறத்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"திரங்குமிவ்","parts":[{"text":"திரங்குமிவ்","lemma":"திரங்குமிவ்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வழங்கல்","parts":[{"text":"வழங்கல்","lemma":"வழங்கல்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஊரே","parts":[{"text":"ஊரே","lemma":"ஊரே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Like the growing crescent moon, successively increasing, / with the distressing disease that made the wrist bangles slip, / having become like crushed foliage and withered, / besides suffering because companions are not near, / the rain also, O friend, has become dark and set. / Even when the fallen rain does not fall, / more than us who grieve on his account, / this bustling village grieves on our account!","translation":"O friend, growing step by step like the waxing moon, my painful distress has made my wrist-bangles slip. Withered and crushed like soft foliage, I suffer because my loved ones are not near. To add to this, the rain-clouds have darkened and poured down. Yet, even when the rain stops falling, this bustling village grieves for our sake, even more than we grieve for him!","modern":"வளர்கின்ற பிறை நிலவைப் போல நாளுக்கு நாள் பெருகி, என் கைவளையல்களைக் கழலச் செய்த துன்பத் துயரத்தோடு, கசக்கிய தளிர் போல வாடி, அருகில் துணையாக இருப்பவர்கள் இல்லாததால் வருந்துவது ஒருபுறமிருக்க, தோழியே! மேகமும் இருண்டு மழை பொழிந்துவிட்டது. பெய்த மழை நின்ற காலத்திலும், அவர் மீது அன்பு கொண்டு வருந்தும் நம்மை விட, இந்த நடமாட்டம் மிகுந்த ஊரார் நம் நிலைமைக்காக அதிகமாக வருந்துகிறார்கள்.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her confidante in the mullai tiṇai (forest landscape), which is associated with patient waiting during the rainy season. She laments that her distress has grown like the waxing moon, causing her to lose weight so that her bangles slip off. She feels crushed and withered like soft foliage, and her suffering is worsened by the absence of her lover just as the dark rain-clouds arrive. However, she notes with a touch of irony that the busy villagers seem to pity her and gossip about her state, grieving for her even more than she herself grieves for her departed lover. The key words are 'வளர்பிறை' (waxing moon), 'நெகிழ்த்த' (loosened), 'சாஅய்' (withered), and 'மழை' (rain).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}